\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\paragraph{Permutation null distribution.}
To confirm that the 31.3\% C rate is not an artifact of the MH procedure, we run 1,000 permutation tests randomly reassigning temporal labels.
The null distribution has mean 0.22\% (SD=0.08\%), with the 99th percentile at 0.48\%.
The observed 31.3\% yields $z=388.5$ ($p<0.001$), confirming the temporal signal is real, though its interpretation (instability vs.\ capability improvement) remains open.

