\subsection{Negative Results and Scope Boundaries}
\label{sec:negative}

We report four classes of negative results that bound the scope of our contributions and motivate future work.

\paragraph{RL robustness.}
Table~\ref{tab:rl} reports detection AUROC across non-RL, alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO, $N=477$), and reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO, $N=13$) model populations.
MH-DIF shows minimal degradation ($\Delta=-0.02$), but all methods perform poorly in absolute terms (MH-DIF AUROC$=0.60$--$0.62$).
The reasoning-RL sample ($N=13$) is too small for statistical conclusions: DeLong test $p=0.23$ and TOST equivalence $p=0.08$ are both non-significant.
Bootstrap CI width of 0.15 reflects this sample limitation.

