\paragraph{Cumulative Bayesian DIF.}
Table~\ref{tab:cumulative} reports simulated detection power under cumulative Bayesian priors \citep{sinharay2006study} across 1--4 administrations.
Power improves from TPR$=0.42$ (single administration, $\delta=1.0$) to TPR$=0.68$ (four administrations), falling short of the 0.70 target.
FPR remains controlled ($\le 0.06$).
This is a simulation-only result under a well-specified 1D IRT model.
Given that real MMLU exhibits severe IRT misfit (98\% $|L_z|>2$), these power estimates are optimistic upper bounds and do not transfer directly to practice.

